(Act as the Senior Frontend Engineer for UniLang.) Tj
T* (TASK: Build the Offline Travel Phrasebook and the Reading & Listening Studio.) Tj
T* (REQUIREMENTS:) Tj
T* (1. Build /src/components/phrasebook/PhrasebookSection.jsx:) Tj
T* (   - Implement the 8 core categories \(Emergency, Medical, Food, Directions, Lodging, Transit, Shopping, Social\) with 50+) Tj
T* (essential phrases per language.) Tj
T* (   - Include rapid-access "Emergency Mode" pinned at the top with red accent styling.) Tj
T* (   - Every phrase must include: English, target script, Romanized phonetics, audio playback button, and "Save to) Tj
T* (Notebook" icon.) Tj
T* (   - Instant search filter indexing English, target script, and phonetics.) Tj
T* (2. Build /src/components/reading/ReadingStudio.jsx:) Tj
T* (   - Dual-language parallel reader displaying side-by-side or stacked synchronized sentences.) Tj
T* (   - Interactive audio player with sentence-level karaoke highlighting as audio advances.) Tj
T* (   - Interactive word tokens: Clicking any word opens a quick definition popover.) Tj
T* (   - 3-question reading comprehension quiz at the end of each passage.) Tj
T* (VERIFICATION: Verify audio-text karaoke synchronization; ensure offline phrasebook accessibility; test mobile) Tj
T* (responsiveness.) Tj
